## Design direction

A smooth, polished pin style that gives color artwork a clean jewelry-like surface and clearly defined metal borders.

For custom imitation hard enamel pins, begin with the part of the artwork that must read first. Keep the outline, smallest lettering, color breaks and functional details clear, then use finish and presentation to support the design rather than compete with it.

## Confirmed choices and project decisions

- Materials include zinc alloy, stainless iron, aluminum, and iron.
- Back treatments include sandblasted, polished, raised or recessed metal logo, and laser marking.
- Backing choices include butterfly, rubber, jewelry and deluxe clutches, magnet, safety pin, long stick pin, and screw with nut.
- Standard packaging is an OPP bag; optional packaging includes a printed backing card, plastic case, and velvet box.

## Preparing your brief

Send the artwork, intended dimensions, quantity, delivery destination and required timing. Note which surfaces, moving parts, attachments or packaging details matter most so the quotation can be based on one clear specification.

Golden One will use the approved brief as the basis for the final product specification; unconfirmed materials, claims and performance details are not assumed.
